; The core: types and laws, and nothing else. Pure - no clock, no
; randomness, no I/O - and under its ceiling, because a core nobody
; read is not a core whose laws are laws.
;
; The strict readers and writers of the formats live in format/, which
; is pure as well but is a codec rather than an algebra: it says how
; the outside is shaped, not what is true. The lint checks both for
; purity and bounds each separately.
(library
 (name mathcoding)
 (wrapped false)
 (modules domain verdict)
 (libraries unix))
